Note that your god's anger is separate from your alignment.  When you
sacrifice a non-aligned unicorn, you improve your alignment, but may
not improve your gods anger one bit.  The "You feel you are 
thoroughly on the right path" message means your alignment has
improved (gotten more strident).

To decrease the gods anger, you use this formula:

#define MAXVALUE 24
u.ugangr -= ((value * (u.ualigntyp == U_CHAOTIC ? 2 : 3)) / MAXVALUE);

Where value is a measure of the monster difficulty (0-24).  For the 
anger to decrease at all, the vaule must be >=8, or >=12 for chaotic 
gods. 

If you're having trouble doing this, it's probably because you're
chaotic.  You could try converting, and then trying to make your
new god happy.

Perhaps someone will post a list of all monsters with a value over
12.  The routine mstrength uses a complex algorithm to calculate
value. It looks like monsters with many attack (particularly
special or weapon attacks) should have high values.  Note that if
a monster seemed inadequate, there's no point trying the same 
monster type again later.  

Also note that it doesn't depend on your level.  If you get your 
god angry on level 1, you still need a big huge sacrifice to 
cheer him up.

Probably the easiest way to make your god happy again is to reverse 
genocide krakens in a sealed off room with an altar and no water.
Without water, they don't attack, and all drop down to 1 hp.  
You can then kill them easily.  They are a big enough sacrifice to 
make even chaotic gods happier.

